  "raw_text": "268\n\nUr waitna\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmale prostitute\n \n/ prostituto\n\nUrhwaia\n \n(\ndb,dictu-alt\n;\n \nUrwaia\n-\ndictu,sn;\n \nUhrwaia\n-\ndict\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto sprout, to bud\n \n/ brotar, retoñar\n\nUrus\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmonkey\n \n/ mono, mico\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nRuskika\n)\n\nUsra\n \n(\ndict,dictu,lv,fy\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwoodlouse, woodworm, termite\n \n/ carcoma, comején Is it commonly used in these ways?\n\nUsupum\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu\n;\n \nUsupam\n-\ndict-alt\n,\ndictu-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \noak tree\n \n/ roble\n\nUsus\n \n(n/s) (\ndict,Raitipura\n \n–\n \ndict also says turkey buzzard\n \n–\n \nsee if it is used this way or for other birds)\n \n–\n \ncrow\n \n/ cuervo\n\nUtla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhouse, building\n \n/ casa, edificio\n\n(Construct:\n \nWaitla\n \n–\n \nmy house\n \n/ mi casa;\n \nWamtla\n \n–\n \nyour house\n \n/ tu casa;\n \nWatla\n \n–\n \nhis/her/their house\n \n/ su casa)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nmuihni bara lakri nani wan watla ra yamni briaia dukiara\n \n–\n \nin order to welcome brothers and sisters to our\nhouse (hospitality)\n \n/ para dar la bienvenida a los hermanos y hermanas en nuestra casa (hospitalidad))\n\nAsla Aidrubanka Watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nKingdom Hall\n \n/\n \nSalón del Reino\n\n(Note/Nota: A Kingdom Hall formerly was called\n \nKingka Lâka Watla\n \n/ Un Salón del Reino se llamaba anteriormente\n \nKingka\nLâka Watla\n)\n\nAidrubanka Watla ra ulbi sakanka bâra ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe books at the Kingdom Hall, Kingdom Hall library\n \n/\nlos libros en el Salón del Reino, biblioteca del Salón del Reino\n\nAsla Aidrubanka Watla Tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nAssembly Hall\n \n/\n \nSalón del Asambleas\n\nBibi watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwomb\n \n/ matriz\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPlauya\n)\n\nIska watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbladder\n \n/ vejiga\n\nLayan nani\n \nwa\ntla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nlions’ den\n \n/ foso de los leones\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb64\n):\n \nDaniel\n \nlayan nani watla ra\n \n–\n \nDaniel in the Lions’ den\n \n/ Daniel en el foso de los leones\n)\n\nPrias watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbuilding where a religious meeting is held, church\n \n/ edificio donde se celebra una reunión\nreligiosa, iglesia\n\nUtla banhta\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroof, roofing, roof of a house, roof of a building\n \n/ techo, techo de una casa, techo de un\nedificio\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb30\n):\n \nWitin ai watla banhta ra biki kakaira nani ra yukukan\n \n–\n \nShe hid the spies on the roof of her house\n \n/ Ella\nescondió a los espías en el techo de su casa)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb79\n):\n \nJisas bâra kan ba kat lahbaia dukiara utla banhta ra unta kum daukan\n \n–\n \nIn order to lower (him) to where\nJesus was, (they) made a hole in the roof\n \n/ Para bajarlo (a él) a donde estaba Jesús, (ellos) hicieron un agujero en el techo)\n\nUtla dawanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhouse owner, householder\n \n/ dueño de casa, amo de casa\n\nUtla dawanka mairin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhousewife, woman householder\n \n/ ama de casa\n\nUtla durka mawanra Baibil stadika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndoorstep Bible study\n \n/ curso bíblico en la puerta\n\nUtla latka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyard, courtyard\n \n/ patio\n\nUtla papakni\n \n–\n \ntemporary dwelling, temporary shelter, hut\n \n/ vivienda temporal, refugio temporal, cabaña\n\nUtla Papakni liliaka ba\n \n–\n \nThe Festival of Booths\n \n/ La Fiesta de las Cabañas\n\nUtla paskaia l\nȃ\nka\n \n(n\n/s\n)\n \n–\n \nconstruction\n \nwork / trabajo de construcci\nó\nn\n\nUtla utla ra smalkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto teach/preach from house to house\n \n/ enseñar/predicar de casa en casa\n\nWaitla uplika\n \n(\ndb\n-\nJ\nasua\n \n24:15\n)\n \n–\n \nmy household\n \n/ mi casa\n, mi familia\n\nWatla âpu\n \n–\n \nhomeless, not having a home\n \n/ sin hogar, no tener un hogar\n\nUya\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nmany, much, so many, so much\n \n/ mucho\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jan 3:16\n):\n \nGâd tasba ra uya latwan kaikan\n \n–\n \nGod loved the world so much\n \n/ D